---
description: Workflow, git safety, and secrets rules (always applied)
alwaysApply: true
---

# SECRETS (hard rules)
- NEVER open, print, summarize, or copy the contents of any .env file.
- NEVER overwrite or recreate an existing .env. If .env.example changes,
  tell me which variable NAMES to add by hand.
- NEVER hardcode keys, passwords, connection strings, tokens, or R2 keys.
- NEVER ask me to paste secrets into chat. If a secret is needed, tell me
  the variable name and say "put it in your local .env".
- .env, .env.*, .vercel, node_modules, .venv, dist must be in .gitignore.
- If you ever see a secret in code or git history, stop and tell me.

# WORKING IN PHASES
- Work one phase at a time. Finish, run it, fix errors, commit, then STOP
  and tell me exactly what to check. Wait for "next".
- Before coding, state your plan in 3-6 lines. Ask at most ONE question, and
  only if you are truly blocked. Otherwise state your assumption and go.
- Prefer the smallest change that solves the problem. Do not refactor
  unrelated code. Do not rename or move files unless asked.
- If a requirement is unclear or risky (money, stock, data loss), say so
  before building it.

# GIT SAFETY
- Two separate repos:
  Frontend: https://github.com/tayyabriaz60/Cloth-Brand.git
  Backend:  https://github.com/tayyabriaz60/Cloth-brand-backend.git
- Before the first push, check the remote. If it is NOT empty (for example an
  older clothing-store project), STOP and tell me. Never overwrite it.
- NEVER force-push. NEVER rewrite history. NEVER commit to main directly if
  I ask for a branch.
- Commit small and often with clear messages:
  feat: ..., fix: ..., refactor: ..., chore: ..., docs: ...
- Do not commit generated files, build output, or secrets.

# DEPENDENCIES
- Do not add a package without asking. If you think one is needed, explain
  why in one sentence and wait.
- Pin versions. Prefer packages that are small and well maintained.

# DEPLOYMENT (Vercel)
- Do NOT log in to Vercel or run deploy commands. Prepare the config and
  list the env var NAMES; I will connect the repos in the Vercel dashboard.
- Deploy order: backend first, then frontend, then set FRONTEND_URL on the
  backend and redeploy it.
- Free-tier reality: the backend may sleep and be slow on the first request.
  Design for it (loading messages, retries), do not fight it.

# COMMUNICATION
- Reply in simple English. Keep answers short. No long essays.
- At the end of each task give: (1) files changed, (2) exact commands to
  run, (3) a 3-step way for me to test it, (4) anything you assumed.
- Be honest. If something is not tested or you are unsure, say so.
  Never claim "done" without running the build/tests.
- Ideas outside the current phase go to BAADMEIN.md, one line each.
